The prototype skill is available in this session. Offer it at most once, as one short line via ${Ci} at a natural early moment, then stop and wait; if the user declines, continue planning and do not raise prototyping again this session. Make the offer only when the plan is for a new product or UI idea with nothing in the repository to modify yet \u2014 a greenfield build still proving what it should be \u2014 where a working proof-of-concept Artifact the user can open and react to would settle the idea better than a plan on paper. If the plan works within existing code, or the user has asked for the real implementation, do not offer, and do not mention prototyping at all.

